  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  _displayedPrefab: {fileID: 0}
  _spinObject: 0
  _allowNonInteractables: 1
  _putBackTime: 2
  _labelText: The Standard Kyudojo
  _infoText: The standard Kyudojo consists of a shooting hall (Shajo), a arrow pathway
    (Yamichi) and a target house (Matoba). The Shajo is a open-faced building with
    a high ceiling. The floor is minimum five meters in width. Between the archers
    is a space at least of 1.8 meters and the shooting distance is twenty-eight meters.
    Every Shajo has a Kamiza (look behind you). The Yamichi is the open ground between
    the two houses and is extremely simple in design. The Motaba is in similar design
    as the Shajo and is also called "Azuchi". It contains a bank of sand that holds
    the targets at a low height, the center is only at 27 cm.
  _infoImage: {fileID: 0}
  _infoAudioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: decf181e345d3824b8e29f4d547edc50, type: 3}
