  m_text: The arrows are called "Ya". They are close to a meter or more and therefore
    really long in contrast to western counterparts. The arrowhead of this arrow
    is a traditional "Yajiri" and is not used in todays kyudo anymore. Todays arrowheads
    are designed more like bullets and are called "Yanone".
